{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <cstdio>\ntypedef long long ll;\nconst ll MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nll read() {\n    ll x = 0, f = 1;\n    int ch;\n    while ((ch = getchar()) < '0' || ch > '9') {\n        if (ch == '-') f = -1;\n    }\n    while (ch >= '0' && ch <= '9') {\n        x = x * 10 + (ch - '0');\n        ch = getchar();\n    }\n    return x * f;\n}\n\nll mul_mod(ll a, ll b, ll m) {\n    ll ans = 0;\n    while (b) {\n        if (b & 1) ans = (ans + a) % m;\n        b >>= 1;\n        a = (a + a) % m;\n    }\n    return ans;\n}\n\nll pow_mod(ll a, ll b, ll m) {\n    ll ans = 1;\n    for (; b; b >>= 1) {\n        if (b & 1) ans = mul_mod(ans, a, m);\n        a = mul_mod(a, a, m);\n    }\n    return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ll p = read();\n    ll k = read();\n    ll ret = 0;\n    switch (k) {\n        case 0:\n            ret = pow_mod(p, p - 1, MOD);\n            break;\n        case 1:\n            ret = pow_mod(p, p, MOD);\n            break;\n        default:\n            if (k > 1) {\n                ll len = 1;\n                ll cur = k;\n                while (cur != 1) {\n                    cur = (ll)(cur * k % p);\n                    ++len;\n                }\n                ret = pow_mod(p, (p - 1) / len, MOD);\n            }\n            break;\n    }\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", ret);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.io.BufferedReader;\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport java.io.InputStreamReader;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n\n    private static long readLong() throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        long x = 0, f = 1;\n        int ch;\n        // Skip non-digit characters\n        while ((ch = reader.read()) != -1) {\n            if (ch >= '0' && ch <= '9') {\n                x = ch - '0';\n                break;\n            } else if (ch == '-') {\n                f = -1;\n            }\n        }\n        if (ch == -1) return 0; // EOF\n        // Read remaining digits\n        while ((ch = reader.read()) != -1 && ch >= '0' && ch <= '9') {\n            x = x * 10 + (ch - '0');\n        }\n        return x * f;\n    }\n\n    private static long mulMod(long a, long b, long m) {\n        long ans = 0;\n        while (b > 0) {\n            if ((b & 1) == 1) {\n                ans = (ans + a) % m;\n            }\n            b >>= 1;\n            a = (a + a) % m;\n        }\n        return ans;\n    }\n\n    private static long powMod(long a, long b, long m) {\n        long ans = 1;\n        while (b > 0) {\n            if ((b & 1) == 1) {\n                ans = mulMod(ans, a, m);\n            }\n            a = mulMod(a, a, m);\n            b >>= 1;\n        }\n        return ans;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long p = readLong();\n        long k = readLong();\n        long ret = 0;\n        if (k == 0) {\n            ret = powMod(p, p - 1, MOD);\n        } else if (k == 1) {\n            ret = powMod(p, p, MOD);\n        } else {\n            long len = 1;\n            long cur = k % p; // ensure cur is modulo p\n            while (cur != 1) {\n                cur = (cur * k) % p;\n                len++;\n            }\n            ret = powMod(p, (p - 1) / len, MOD);\n        }\n        System.out.println(ret);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.15369614958763123, -0.00416305148974061, -1.311301275563892e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.90866428258596e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, 0.0, -6.198863957251888e-06, -0.3156868517398834, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.014164154417812824, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -4.541770613286644e-05, -0.02054867334663868, -9.893881360767409e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.005774364341050386, -0.004081491846591234, -7.712543447269127e-05, -0.47621604800224304, -1.0132738680113107e-05, -8.105902816168964e-05, -0.00010132275929208845, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0001234931987710297, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.264974000354414e-06, -0.018174778670072556, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.13992838561534882, -4.768360213347478e-06, -0.0044939713552594185, -0.011519819498062134, -0.0791541114449501, -0.005239089950919151, -0.02975226752460003, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.16252636909484863, -0.5760571360588074, 0.0, -5.006777428206988e-06, 0.0, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -5.2689116273541003e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -0.9924805164337158, -0.0004655231023207307, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.2551199197769165, -0.003179615829139948, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.264974000354414e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.924526340095326e-05, -1.1086402082582936e-05, -0.04859720915555954, -2.50339189733495e-06, -0.3329243